{
  "id": "Compound::DB01326 - Gene::55867",
  "verbalization": "Cefamandole, a broad-spectrum antibiotic, is linked to Slc22a11 through a series of molecular interactions that ultimately involve the Sodium-independent Organic Anion Transmembrane Transporter Activity. The evidence suggests that Cefamandole binds to Slc22a7 or Slc22a8, which are both involved in organic anion transport. These transporters, in turn, are part of the broader Sodium-independent Organic Anion Transmembrane Transporter Activity, which is directly associated with Slc22a11. This indicates that Cefamandole may influence the activity of Slc22a11 through a pathway involving organic anion transport. The consistent binding of Cefamandole to Slc22a7 or Slc22a8, along with the shared participation in the same transport activity, suggests a potential mechanism by which Cefamandole could modulate Slc22a11 function. The evidence supports a plausible, though not yet fully elucidated, relationship between Cefamandole and Slc22a11, mediated through the organic anion transport pathway.",
